{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor performed strong neonatal vomiting risk screening, repeatedly gave correct emergency thresholds, and escalated appropriately when feeding/urine concerns persisted. However, after the family disclosed “卵圆孔未闭、外阴血管瘤,” the doctor never provided the required privacy-friendly follow-up reminder or hemangioma return precautions, and the home plan did not explicitly separate the two twins’ feeding/urine/symptom/medication records. These are responsibility-chain omissions without a serious unsafe error, so the grade is capped at 2 despite meaningful strengths and some high-order repair.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00287",
        "explanation": "The last doctor plan gave concrete return thresholds for feeding, urine, and red flags.",
        "quote": "任何时候立即急诊"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00301",
        "explanation": "The trajectory ended with the family still seeking final confirmation rather than a doctor closing the loop.",
        "quote": "最后再确认一下"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The acute vomiting/feeding/urine plan was largely executable and traceable, but closure remained questionable because the final family confirmation was not answered and required non-acute diagnosis follow-up and twin-specific separation were not fully closed.",
    "label": "questionable_open",
    "safe": false,
    "traceable": true
  },
